{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvKNk7qVT4Ddu5Tup1dQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The limit applies to the **compressed (gzip) size** of your Worker, not the raw size. Wrangler prints both after a build or `--dry-run` (`Total Upload: … KiB / gzip: … KiB`), and the gzip number is the one checked against the limit. That limit is **3 MB on the Workers Free plan and 10 MB on the Paid plan**. Separately, the uncompressed bundle can't be larger than 64 MB.\n\nThis comes from what I know about Cloudflare's published limits, not from a docs check today, and the project's Ludion lessons don't mention it. If you're close to the line, confirm the current numbers on the Workers \"Limits\" page. To see where the size comes from, `wrangler deploy --dry-run --outdir dist --metafile` shows which dependencies take up the most space."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8618,"cache_read_input_tokens":15764,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8618},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"606c75bc-2b83-4860-a606-eae016982964","uuid":"1af762f0-f746-4f47-bc10-1d826522c00c","timestamp":"2026-10-11T10:47:58.949Z","request_id":"req_011CfvKNjsTHmWbUhs9YuwN6"}
